   "evidence": "Amplitude.lean:72 `@[expose] public section` vs Operator.lean:48 `public section` / :50 `noncomputable section`, which pairs `def dipoleS` (:63) with `dipoleS_def ... := (rfl)` (:66-68) and keeps the body unexposed.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/SmallX/Dipole/Amplitude.lean",
   "fix": "Use `public section` (plus `noncomputable section`) without `@[expose]`, as the sibling `Dipole/Operator.lean:48` does; in-file proofs that unfold the defs are unaffected, since `@[expose]` only governs other modules.",
   "issue": "`@[expose] public section` exposes the bodies of `blackDisc` (:131) and `golecBiernatWusthoff` (:156) downstream, so consumers can unfold them by defeq. No consumer needs to: `blackDisc_apply_self`/`blackDisc_apply_ne` cover all cases, and `golecBiernatWusthoff_def`/`one_sub_golecBiernatWusthoff` give the value and the S-matrix. With the body exposed, the deliberate `:= (rfl)` at :162 buys nothing.",
   "line": "72"
  },
  {
   "evidence": "Amplitude.lean:145-149 proves the identity-kernel fact inline; the parallel `@[simp] one_sub_golecBiernatWusthoff` at :166-169 is public, so the file develops both sides but exports only one.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/SmallX/Dipole/Amplitude.lean",
   "fix": "Pull `e` out as a public lemma, e.g. `one_sub_blackDisc : (Matrix.of fun x y => 1 - blackDisc x y) = (1 : Matrix (EuclideanSpace \u211d (Fin 2)) _ \u211d)` (or the pointwise `@[simp]` form), and use it in `isAdmissible_blackDisc`.",
   "issue": "The black disc's characteristic S-matrix identity \u2014 `Matrix.of (fun x y => 1 - blackDisc x y) = 1`, claimed in three docstrings (:47-48, :127, :142) \u2014 is proved only as the local `have e` inside `isAdmissible_blackDisc` and never exposed, while the same interaction is exposed for the other witness as `one_sub_golecBiernatWusthoff` (:166). A consumer must re-derive it.",
   "line": "143"
  }
 ],
